    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d569">

                <pb facs="0615" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg503"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Fox to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-11-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 28, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 784.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, respectfully referring to
                    my telegram of November 25,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d569-f1"/> to inclose herewith
                    copy of the note, with translation, transcribing to me the telegram from the
                    Spanish minister for foreign affairs to minister for foreign affairs of Ecuador,
                    in which it is stated that His Majesty the King of Spain had declined to act
                    further as arbitrator in the boundary dispute between Ecuador and Peru.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams C. Fox.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d569-a1.xml" xpointer="d569-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
